[%# Errors raised by the IssueTypeWorkflow extension. %]

[% IF error == "issue_type_required" %]
  [% title = "Issue Type Required" %]
  Every new item must be filed as either a <em>BUG</em> or a <em>REQUIREMENT</em>.
  Please set the <em>Issue Type</em> field. (Items filed before this field
  existed have no type and are treated as bugs; they are not affected.)

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_unknown" %]
  [% title = "Unknown Issue Type" %]
  <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em> is not a known issue type.

[% ELSIF error == "issue_category_mismatch" %]
  [% title = "Category Does Not Match Issue Type" %]
  The category <em>[% category FILTER html %]</em> does not belong to issue type
  <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em>. Leaving the category empty is always
  allowed. This is not a permissions problem - no account can put a category of
  one issue type on an item of the other.
  [% IF allowed.size %]
    <p>Allowed for <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em>:
    [% FOREACH c = allowed %]<em>[% c FILTER html %]</em>[% ', ' UNLESS loop.last %][% END %].</p>
  [% END %]

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_resolution_mismatch" %]
  [% title = "Resolution Does Not Match Issue Type" %]
  <em>[% resolution FILTER html %]</em> is not a resolution an item of type
  <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em> can be closed with.
  [%# Listed from the policy itself. Spelling the sets out by hand is how this
      message came to claim a bug could only be FIXED, when INVALID, WONTFIX,
      DUPLICATE and WORKSFORME are equally allowed. %]
  [% IF allowed.size %]
    Allowed for <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em>:
    [% FOREACH r = allowed %]<em>[% r FILTER html %]</em>[% ', ' UNLESS loop.last %][% END %].
  [% END %]
  This is not a permissions problem - no account can set it.

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_initial_status_unavailable" %]
  [% title = "Lifecycle Entry Point Missing" %]
  Items of type <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em> must be created in status
  <em>[% status FILTER html %]</em>, but that is not currently a legal status
  for a new item. The status workflow no longer matches the configured
  lifecycles - re-run <em>setup-projects.pl</em>.

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_initial_status_needs_comment" %]
  [% title = "Comment Required" %]
  Items of type <em>[% issue_type FILTER html %]</em> are created in status
  <em>[% status FILTER html %]</em>, and the workflow requires a comment for
  that transition. Please describe the item.

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_workflow_misconfigured" %]
  [% title = "Issue Type Workflow Is Misconfigured" %]
  Part of the configuration the issue-type lifecycles depend on is missing or
  has been altered - the category field, a category value, a product, a status
  or the status workflow itself. Changes are blocked until
  <em>setup-projects.pl</em> has been re-run. This is deliberate: the
  alternative would be to silently stop enforcing the lifecycles.

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_value_rename_forbidden" %]
  [% title = "That Value Cannot Be Renamed" %]
  <em>[% value FILTER html %]</em> is part of the configured issue-type
  lifecycles. Renaming a <em>[% field FILTER html %]</em> value rewrites it on
  every item already using it, directly in the database - so it is refused here.
  Change <em>expected-state.json</em> and re-run <em>setup-projects.pl</em>
  instead.

[% ELSIF error == "issue_type_value_delete_forbidden" %]
  [% title = "That Value Cannot Be Deleted" %]
  <em>[% value FILTER html %]</em> is part of the configured issue-type
  lifecycles, so deleting it takes a configured lifecycle value away and no
  future item could be filed with it. (Bugzilla separately refuses to delete a
  value that items are still using; this refusal covers the ones that are
  currently unused.) Change <em>expected-state.json</em> and re-run
  <em>setup-projects.pl</em>.

[% END %]
